From 7404fa6a7c8c43a467bf912672d4536602df8707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(indoor): explicit door reviews take precedence over
 native-cell matching

In native-cell mode directoryDoorReviews chose the automatic portal before
consulting explicitReviews. A semantic ownership link rejected upstream
(absent from the accepted links, present in explicitReviews) stayed
unmatched under legacy, but native mode filled it and reported it as
connected with hasExplicitReview and nativeOwners.decided both true.

Now an accepted link is applied as written, and a rejected review keeps
the legacy outcome: the native rule never fills or re-owns it, even with
overrideLegacy. nativeOwners.decided is false for any explicitly reviewed
door, and nativeOwners.explicitReview records the status, a reason and the
unchanged link (rooms and semantic source identity). Automatic native
filling applies only where no explicit review exists. Legacy mode output is
unchanged.

Correct the maxOwnerGapFeet comment. The 2 ft native bound is measured from
a side probe beyond the door face with no XY envelope. It is not the legacy
centre-plus-envelope reach and can accept outlines legacy rejects. A new
test pins the 2.1 ft / 1.75 ft example and the 2.35 ft thin-wall edge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F5YScMjv2Mnt4v2xjsTFru
